{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNiXKTJLP73x1D6ijtq3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I judged TC-055 and recorded a **pass**: `OUTCOME: RECORDED result=pass`.\n\n**What I judged.** I'm Claude, the same model family that wrote the dashboard code, so I did not give the approval myself. I checked the six Codex Luna judges' sitting against the Method, using their raw files in `review-tmp/2026-10-25a-leg19/rj920/` rather than the record's summary:\n\n- **HEAD still matches what was shot.** Since the render base `825dd47`, the only change is the review record. I rebuilt `PROJECT_STATE.html` at HEAD: only the as-of stamp differed, and it still reads `825dd47de`. I then restored the committed file.\n- **The briefs are complete and clean.** The rubric section in a judge's brief is byte-identical to the rubric at HEAD. The briefs are generated by one script that reads every quote from the registries at HEAD: SN-023/024, SR-054, LLR-055, TC-055 and the six test-bound rows with their TC ids. None carries the implementers' self-assessment or an earlier verdict.\n- **The matrix was complete.** The shoot produced 36 shots, with no tab reported \"NOT shot\" and Knowledge skipped because its dial is off. My own script confirmed that the 328 tiles are each at most 1500 px a side and add up exactly to every shot's area. Each brief lists every tile in its manifest, and the launch script attaches each of them.\n- **The judges actually looked at the images.** Token use rose with tile count (about 74k, 115k and 150k for 44, 48 and 72 tiles), even though the sessions ran only 29–43 s.\n- **The verdicts cite only live anchors.** All six end `APPROVE findings=0` with T2, T4, T5 and T8 passing, and none cites a retired anchor. Every tile a judge cites is in its own manifest. T5 was judged in both themes, by three judges each.\n- **The retired anchors stay covered by tests.** All ten tests behind the retired anchors and the test-held parts of the live ones are Approved and linked to their low-level requirements.\n- **My own look at five tiles** found nothing that contradicts T2, T4, T5 or T8.\n\n**Departures, written into the verdict:**\n- No judge could run any command: the Codex sandbox failed every one. So unlike the previous re-judge (WI-831), no judge cross-checked against `PROJECT_STATE.html`; they judged from the brief and tiles alone. The Method doesn't require that read, so I counted the point as met but marked it.\n- Each judge's pass rests on the one to five tiles it cites per anchor, so it is a sample of its cell.\n- In the dark-theme roadmap, the wires are faint. None of the live anchors' remaining clauses covers wire visibility, so it doesn't affect the result.\n\n**Commits in lane `wi-920`** (all commit hooks passed):\n- `9436c807b` adds the record `docs/test/observations/TC-055.2026-10-25T092405Z.toml`. It is a pass that expires 2027-01-23, and its inputs digest is unchanged from the work item's spec.\n- `0d9b11f46` adds the verdict `docs/reviews/wi-920/002-ADJUDICATE-3cef50b.md` and its `.requested` file, with the `WI: WI-920` and `Loop-Session` trailers.\n\nI did not edit the test-case registry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":91938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"output_tokens":741,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d95662c-69a9-4992-bb0d-a208dbf4b867","uuid":"06350397-9002-402c-8fae-14394106d7ae","timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:27:04.295Z","request_id":"req_011CgNiXJp6Yoq8orhjbCLKr"}
